+## Source-defined kernel-local alternatives
+
+`lib/alternatives.ass` derives eliminator-encoded Either/Maybe choices from ordinary
+staged closures. Dynamic constructor choice reuses the existing callable conditional
+plan and elimination specializes before the concrete emitter. This adds no parser
+form, callable primitive, runtime tag object, guest allocation or ABI layout. Rank-1
+inference means the encoding is intentionally kernel-local rather than a genuine
+higher-rank or storable sum type; callable alternatives must be eliminated before
+ASABI or stream-element boundaries. See [the contract](ALTERNATIVES.md) and
+[validation](ALTERNATIVES-VALIDATION.md).
+
